        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Tien Len',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Tien Len (Tiáº¿n LÃªn), often called 'Thirteen' or 'Killer 13', is the national card game of Vietnam. It is a climbing/shedding game similar to Big Two and President. Players race to empty their hands by playing combinations that beat the previous play. The Two (Heo) is the highest card, and special 'bombs' can beat Twos.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Tiến lên is a shedding-type card game originating in Vietnam and is often considered Vietnam's national card game. It is common in Vietnamese and Vietnamese-American communities and spread to the United States and Australia with migration. It is related to Chinese climbing games such as Big Two and Dou dizhu.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2-4 (typically 4).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card. Rank: 3(low)-4-5...K-A-2(high). Suit Rank: Spades < Clubs < Diamonds < Hearts.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Deal all 13 cards to each player.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
